      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Neither SGLT2 inhibitors nor GLP-1 receptor agonists have replaced metformin as the universal first-line therapy for type 2 diabetes . Current clinical guidelines from organizations like the American Diabetes Association (ADA) still recommend metformin and lifestyle modifications as the traditional foundation, though both SGLT2s and GLP-1s can be used as first-line therapy in specific high-risk patient populations (such as those with established atherosclerotic cardiovascular disease, heart failure, or chronic kidney disease).",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
